(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Tree-level gravitational scattering of two scalars", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"dc9fa314-8461-47a9-99a4-40565efd709a"],

Cell["\<\
Build the exchange amplitude for two distinguishable massive scalars, convert \
it to a center-of-mass differential cross section, and check the \
nonrelativistic limit.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ffac651-9e08-4986-8274-61357ac7f5ad"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d3192615-35de-4b5f-94e2-39c60d4277f4"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e1b93f4a-0cc5-453b-a7bf-0c782d10ec56"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000101062944523*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4515f81e-b61a-4241-a539-2cbe98bbcb95"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook requires FORM on the kernel\[CloseCurlyQuote]s PATH. \
CalcFormCalculate performs bosonic algebra and Lorentz contractions; TFORM is \
used automatically when available. FeynCalc handles loop reduction and any \
Dirac or colour algebra before the bosonic coefficients are sent to FORM.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.000101086781893*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4a8d65e3-6ce6-4c02-87ff-\
e16879c1c9ec"],

Cell["\<\
FeynGrav supplies the vertex and propagator normalisations, including i and \
\[Kappa]. The default gravitational gauge parameter is GaugeFixingEpsilon = \
2. The displayed diagram weights are retained from the original example; the \
notebook does not derive their combinatorics.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1633e35a-7106-4b20-bb85-7f917f324481"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Fix the external kinematics", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9bc80cca-f19c-4ecd-b9f6-2a8b989c053a"],

Cell["\<\
SetMandelstam uses all-incoming momenta: p1 + p2 + p3 + p4 = 0. Physical \
outgoing momenta are -p3 and -p4. The masses are {m1, m2, m1, m2}; s + t + u \
= 2 m1\.b2 + 2 m2\.b2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01620e23-85a0-4523-8004-63427842b0cd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SetMandelstam", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "s", ",", "t", ",", "u", ",", "p1", ",", "p2", ",", "p3", ",", "p4", ",", 
    "m1", ",", "m2", ",", "m1", ",", "m2"}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f7febe59-e156-4048-a991-f1fb6e574b20"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Construct the exchange amplitude", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"599f55d5-4f28-4795-8e57-81577b5f7fe4"],

Cell["\<\
Each GravitonScalarVertex has an index pair, two incoming scalar momenta and \
a mass. Join the vertices with a graviton propagator carrying p1 + p3, the \
t-channel momentum. The amplitude retains the factors of i in the Feynman \
rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c78b6f2-b5a5-4d26-af16-207e131b8cc2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalM]", "=", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "}"}], ",", "p1", ",", "p3", ",", 
        "m1"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit", "[", 
       RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
         RowBox[{"p1", "+", "p3"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], ",", "p2", ",", "p4", ",",
         "m2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"u", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"]}], ")"}]}], "-", "s", "-", "t"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"94425197-bc9f-4ad2-99e3-3f0e012cea09"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Convert to center-of-mass variables", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a6cb08aa-8fa6-4f4f-8a70-574997efe030"],

Cell["\<\
p is now the positive magnitude of the three-momentum, rather than a \
four-vector. \[Theta] is the scattering angle; m1 and m2 are positive. These \
assumptions are local to this fresh-kernel example.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e7c1bf8-9ba7-4e0f-a79f-3b2dff7548f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"m1", ">", "0"}], "&&", 
    RowBox[{"m2", ">", "0"}], "&&", 
    RowBox[{"p", ">", "0"}], "&&", 
    RowBox[{"0", "<", "\[Theta]", "<", "\[Pi]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7a60ef80-165f-4903-9cb3-daf9f3b360ed"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Phase space and incoming flux", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"645a3519-c24d-4091-9ea9-2cd4ccca2c9a"],

Cell["\<\
Integrate the final radial momentum k using the energy-conserving delta \
function, retaining the solid angle. The result is \
d\[Sigma]/d\[CapitalOmega], not an angle-integrated total cross section. The \
forward gravitational singularity at \[Theta] = 0 is excluded by the \
assumptions. This symbolic integration may take longer than the amplitude \
contraction.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ce5b74d-09a8-48a9-b5dc-219ad4234f19"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"differentialCrossSection", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SqrtBox[
          RowBox[{
           SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
           SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]], " ", 
         SqrtBox[
          RowBox[{
           SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
           SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]"], 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox[
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"DiracDelta", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              SqrtBox[
               RowBox[{
                SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
                SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]], "+", 
              SqrtBox[
               RowBox[{
                SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
                SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]], "-", 
              SqrtBox[
               RowBox[{
                SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
                SuperscriptBox["k", "2"]}]], "-", 
              SqrtBox[
               RowBox[{
                SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
                SuperscriptBox["k", "2"]}]]}], "]"}], " ", 
            SuperscriptBox[
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}], "4"], " ", 
            SuperscriptBox["k", "2"], " ", 
            SuperscriptBox[
             RowBox[{"(", 
              FractionBox["1", 
               SuperscriptBox[
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}], ")"}], "3"]], ")"}], "2"]}], 
           RowBox[{"16", " ", 
            SqrtBox[
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
              SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]], " ", 
            SqrtBox[
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
              SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]], " ", 
            SqrtBox[
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
              SuperscriptBox["k", "2"]}]], " ", 
            SqrtBox[
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
              SuperscriptBox["k", "2"]}]]}]], 
          RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "k"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"ComplexConjugate", "[", "\[ScriptCapitalM]", "]"}], " ", 
       "\[ScriptCapitalM]"}], 
      SqrtBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", 
          SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"]}], " ", 
         SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"]}], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SuperscriptBox["p", "2"], "+", 
           SqrtBox[
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
               SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
               SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}], ")"}]}]]}], ")"}], "2"]}]]], "/.", 
     "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"s", "\[Rule]", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           SqrtBox[
            RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], "+", 
             SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]], "+", 
           SqrtBox[
            RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"], "+", 
             SuperscriptBox["p", "2"]}]]}], ")"}], "2"]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "4"}], " ", 
         SuperscriptBox["p", "2"], " ", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
           FractionBox["\[Theta]", "2"], "]"}], "2"]}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"\[Kappa]", "\[Rule]", 
        SqrtBox[
         RowBox[{"32", " ", "\[Pi]", " ", "G"}]]}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6a336cdb-d961-40ec-b731-1701740422b1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Display the differential cross section", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3593c57d-60e9-425b-a599-b009d54b119e"],

Cell["\<\
This is the leading tree-level contribution, of order G\.b2. The replacement \
\[Kappa] = \[Sqrt](32 \[Pi] G) is applied when converting the squared \
amplitude to the cross section.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6205defe-6000-4341-903b-c1462fb47f5b"],

Cell[BoxData["differentialCrossSection"], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"efa7e665-ecb1-4be1-91fc-45c37de0167e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Check the nonrelativistic limit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f7d327e3-4060-40bc-a9c0-bd176427e62a"],

Cell["\<\
The leading p \[RightArrow] 0 term is compared with the gravitational \
Rutherford expression. The equality should evaluate to True.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b41235d7-1263-4cf7-becb-adbd6c6dc7b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rutherfordLimitCheck1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Asymptotic", "[", 
       RowBox[{"differentialCrossSection", ",", 
        RowBox[{"p", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["G", "2"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["m1", "2"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["m2", "2"]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox["1", "m1"], "+", 
          FractionBox["1", "m2"]}], ")"}], "2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         SuperscriptBox["p", "4"], " ", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
           FractionBox["\[Theta]", "2"], "]"}], "4"]}], ")"}]}]]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"03e82b1a-6908-46d7-9344-84e87d6caac4"],

Cell[BoxData["rutherfordLimitCheck1"], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5c213f87-1948-48f6-89c3-af25a19f94fe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Expand beyond the leading term", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"cecbb9c1-7cc3-4a60-ada3-74df7ab95ecd"],

Cell["\<\
Series keeps the order term explicitly. Negative powers of p occur because \
the leading long-range scattering cross section grows as p\:207b\:2074.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f34a9239-0a58-44de-b623-bd5ce66fd552"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "/@", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{"differentialCrossSection", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"p", ",", "0", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ebadf493-9dca-4d59-9d0e-339a073488be"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["How to adapt this example", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ea7360aa-5b67-41ee-b7ec-61ce35c090ac"],

Cell["\<\
Change one ingredient at a time: a mass, a momentum assignment, or a vertex \
order. Restart the kernel before rerunning with different kinematics, because \
scalar-product definitions and assumptions persist in the session. \
Re-evaluate all dependent cells after a change. Inspect the stored \
intermediate expressions if a comparison is False or remains unevaluated; do \
not treat an unresolved expression as a passed check.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e06d1cca-e319-44c5-a3dd-3325d4d9a539"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
